SUMMARY:Vertebrates & Invertebrates with Lancaster County Parks Naturalist
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260615T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260615T110000
UID:a291cc1856b7dbfdcbe7e24b7b5c1822@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Discussion\, Presentation\, Storytime\, Summer Rea
 ding\, Toddlers\, Children\, Tweens\n\nDiscover the amazing world of anima
 ls by looking at what’s inside! Animals with a sturdy backbone and a ske
 leton are called vertebrates\, like leaping frogs\, soaring birds\, and ev
 en you.On the flip side\, invertebrates are the "spineless" superstars of 
 nature—like wiggly worms and crunchy beetles—who make up almost all th
 e animals on Earth! Whether they have a hard outer shell for protection or
  a flexible body for squishing into tiny spaces\, every animal has a speci
 al shape that helps it survive and thrive in the wild.
LOCATION:Manheim Community\, MAN Kreider Cultural Center
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/vertebrates-invertebrate
 s-lancaster-county-parks-naturalist-172145
