BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stegosaurus to Steam by Railroad Museum of Pennsylvania
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260616T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260616T140000
UID:ba635177d4a554e01b75f1a409356996@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nHow did giant dinosaurs 
 and ancient forests help power Pennsylvania's mighty trains? Join educator
 s from the Railroad Museum of Pennsylvania for an exciting\, hands-on jour
 ney through time! In this interactive program\, kids will explore fossils\
 , examine pieces of coal\, and discover how plants and creatures from mill
 ions of years ago transformed into the "black rock" that fueled steam engi
 nes across our state. Along the way\, they'll learn how coal formed\, why 
 it was so important to Pennsylvania's history and how it powered the train
 s that connected communities and built industries.Kids can come and learn 
 how we go from dinosaurs and ancient plants to the coal that powers the tr
 ains in our museum. They will interact with fossils\, coal\, and culminate
  with seeing a model steam engine run. Ideal for school-age children (Ages
  7-12) and their families\, this program is perfect for curious minds who 
 love dinosaurs\, trains\, history\, and hands-on learning.Registration for
  Stegosaurus to Steam presented by the Railroad Museum of Pennsylvania wil
 l open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 3rd for Manheim Township and East Lam
 peter residents and on Wednesday\, June 10th for residents of other munici
 palities.Registration Requirements – To help us manage our space\, pleas
 e register every person who will be attending\, including adults or siblin
 gs.*For the safety and supervision of all participants: Children under 8 y
 ears old must be accompanied by an adult throughout the program. Children 
 ages 8 and older are welcome to attend the program independently. Library 
 Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration f
 or more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registe
 ring for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel
  your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to 
 allow for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in regi
 stration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the st
 art of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The progr
 am will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot wi
 ll be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If sp
 ots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, regist
 rants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start 
 time. Photography - The Manheim Township Public Library Code of Conduct Po
 licy prohibits photographing or video recording individuals (including chi
 ldren) without their consent (or in the case of a child\, the consent of a
  parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center C
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/stegosaurus-steam-railro
 ad-museum-pennsylvania-161726
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
