BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:History Adventures with Uncharted Lancaster!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260623T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260623T150000
UID:7b5f43265bd5be7acfe14431d596d0f1@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Presentation\, STEM\, Summer Reading\, Toddlers\, Children\, T
 eens\, Adults\, Everyone\n\nAll ages\, please register every person attend
 ing. Children under 8 must be accompanied by a responsible adult. Space is
  limited.Join us for an afternoon that’s equal parts storytelling\, hist
 ory\, and hands-on discovery. We welcome back Adam Zurn\, local author/edu
 cator/blogger/entertainer/adventurer for a special opportunity to allow us
  all to experience being adventurers!Start with a reading of Adam's new bo
 ok\, Canassatego and His Six Arrows based on real events that happened rig
 ht here in Lancaster\, Pennsylvania.Following the story\, Adam will lead a
  show-and-tell segment where kids can get up close with the tools of the t
 rade. He will unpack his modern-day adventurer’s backpack and share the 
 gear he uses when trekking through dark culverts\, riverside cliffs\, and 
 ruins across Lancaster County. Curious minds can ask questions and even ha
 ndle the equipment!Next up\, it’s time for hands-on discovery! One of th
 e interactive stations set up for young adventurers will be a Petroglyph R
 ubbing Station. Inspired by the ancient Safe Harbor petroglyphs\, children
  can create crayon rubbings from laser-engraved replica carvings of these 
 mysterious Native American rock designs.Adventures beneath the surface awa
 it at your library! There will be opportunties to purchase copies of Adam'
 s book that will also support our library!
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL C.X. Carlson Cultural Room
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/hold-adam-zurn-kids-prog
 ram-159741
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
