UID:4f52e416ab284ffa4fa822d75b84f171@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Gaming\, Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\, Teens\n\nJoin th
 e Manheim Township High School Chess Team for an exciting Summer Chess Clu
 b at the Manheim Township Public Library! Whether you're a total beginner 
 or a future grandmaster\, this is the perfect place to learn\, play\, and 
 sharpen your skills in a fun\, friendly atmosphere.🌟 All skill levels w
 elcome!♟ Ages 6-14🧠 Challenge yourself\, make new friends\, and maste
 r the game!Chess sets will be provided—just bring your love for the game
  (or your curiosity to learn)!Ready to make your move? See you there! ♟
 ✨Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 10th for Manheim T
 ownship and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, June 17th for resid
 ents of other municipalities. Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons 
 failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a
  month will be restricted from registering for future programs for a perio
 d of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours
  prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list 
 to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Pl
 ease arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for park
 ing and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the design
 ated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait
  list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allo
 wed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter
  the program 5 minutes past the start time.Drop Off Program – This progr
 am is intended for children over the age of 6 years who can participate in
 dependently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child with youth service
 s staff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the event space. *
 For children ages 6–7\, this is a drop-off program\; however\, a parent 
 or caregiver must remain nearby and wait outside the program room for the 
 duration of the program.In accordance with library policy\, children ages 
 8 and up may be in the library unaccompanied.Designated Ages – Please ad
 here to the age restrictions designated on your registration. Only childre
 n in that age range will be admitted.Photography - The Manheim Township Pu
 blic Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video recor
 ding individuals (including children) without their consent (or in the cas
 e of a child\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center A
