 y stewardship!This fun and educational event will feature an engaging stor
 y along with hands-on activities like the "Honey Bee Waggle" dance\, makin
 g learning about pollinators exciting for kids and adults alike. Plus\, ev
 ery participating family will receive a packet of native wildflower seeds 
 to help support pollinators in their own gardens.For children ages 4-8\, a
 ccompanied by an adult. Registration Requirements – To help us manage ou
 r space\, please register every person who will be attending\, including a
 dults or siblings.Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 24t
 h for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Friday\, July 1s
 t for residents of other municipalities.Library PoliciesNo Show – Patron
 s failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in
  a month will be restricted from registering for future programs for a per
 iod of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hou
 rs prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the waiting lis
 t to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – 
 Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for pa
 rking and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the desi
 gnated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wa
 it list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be al
 lowed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to ent
 er the program 5 minutes past the start time.Accompanying Adults – Thi
 s program is for adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan to att
 end and be engaged with your child. Drop offs will not be permitted. Cance
 llations- Please check your email prior to departing to verify that the pr
 ogram has not been cancelled.Photography - The Manheim Township Public Lib
 rary Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video recording ind
 ividuals (including children) without their consent (or in the case of a c
