 s sea of water was teeming with life and evidence of that can still be fou
 nd today! Learn\, hands-on\, just what PA looked like 400+ million years a
 go\, see real fossils that have been found here\, and learn about our stat
 e fossil\, the trilobite. Participants will then work together to put toge
 ther a big (paper) dinosaur! 🦖Registration for Pennsylvania Paleontolog
 y by Lancaster County Parks will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 8th fo
 r Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, July 15t
 h for residents of other municipalities.Registration Requirements – To h
 elp us manage our space\, please register every person who will be attendi
 ng\, including adults or siblings. Accompanying Adults – This program 
