DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260812T174500
UID:00b49ba5efe3bbe4ca37c867f2de8408@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Storytime\, Children\n\nSummer is here- our planters need our 
 attention!  Join us on our patio for our exciting garden time!  (Rain or s
 hine - if it's raining\, we'll be meeting indoors and limit our outside ti
 me.)  We'll get our hands dirty in the planters\, do some crafts\, and may
 be even read a story!  We'll supply the seeds\, the tools\, gloves\, and t
 he planters.  Plan on getting a little dirty.  This program is for childre
 n ages 6 - 9 years old.  Designated Ages – Please adhere to the age re
 strictions designated on your registration. Only children in that age rang
 e will be admitted.   Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, 
 July 29th for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesda
 y\, August 5th for residents of other municipalities.Drop Off Program –
  This program is intended for children over the age of 6 years who can p
 articipate independently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child with 
 youth services staff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the e
 vent space.  *For children ages 6–7\, this is a drop-off program\; h
 owever\, a parent or caregiver must remain nearby and wait outside the p
 rogram room for the duration of the program. Cancellations- Please check
  your email prior to departing to verify that the program has not been can
 celled. Library Program Policies No Show – Patrons failing to cancel t
 heir registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will be rest
 ricted from registering for future programs for a period of one month’s 
 time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start
  of the program to allow those on the waiting list to be notified of their
  change in registration status. Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minut
 es prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other ci
 rcumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At th
 is time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will b
 e granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the pro
 gram. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program
  5 minutes past the start time. Photography - The Manheim Township Public 
 Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video recording 
 individuals (including children) without their consent (or in the case of 
 a child\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Patio
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/kids-garden-club-177381
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
